    "In patients with arrhythmia-induced cardiomyopathy and HFrEF, the ideal target heart rate for rate control remains uncertain. A stricter rate-control strategy may be necessary due to negative impacts of rapid ventricular rates on HF and cardiomyopathy. Strict rate control is advised for patients with ICDs and CRT. Observational studies suggest AVNA and His bundle pacing improves functional class but may increase pacing thresholds. Nonhydropyridine calcium channel blockers (diltiazem and verapamil) may not be tolerated in HFrEF due to increased morbidity risk. The ANDROMEDA study showed higher mortality in dronedarone group due to worsening HF.": []
